      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I'd like to add this is happening on both Streaming Assistant v9.5.6.2 that a lot of Pico 4 Pro users still use as it's simpler and less volatile than the new streaming assistant Pico connect, but it also happens on the new one too so I'm guessing it's an incompatibility with the latest SteamVR update & VRChat, I get the proper Pico Model controller within SteamVR and the bindings are correct but inside VRChat when launching first time I would get no bindings at all or the default Vive Wand bindings, having to restart VRChat not even re assigning the bindings in SteamVR fixes it; as you might know Pico controllers quite often mimic Oculus cv1 rift controller scheme as it's very similar, if you used through Virtual Desktop usually it will just mirror whatever meta controller without issue but using SA/Pico Connect doesn't. Though that is not an option for me as I use this headset for Face Tracking, something that VD doesn't have yet, as Pico doesn't run A11 neither have the XR elements exposed like Meta Qpro.\n\nI didn't want to open a different ticket since the issue is very similar and related, since this update was this month compared to what was a month ago.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
